275
00:15:36.565 --> 00:15:38.504
Look Jay. The candles work.

276
00:15:40.374 --> 00:15:43.903
Yeah but we're still
stuck taking the bus.

277
00:15:43.943 --> 00:15:45.402
Maybe not.

278
00:15:45.442 --> 00:15:49.171
I lit candle number 1 and wish
number 1 on my list came true.

279
00:15:49.211 --> 00:15:50.910
I think the numbers
on the candles

280
00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:53.639
correspond with the numbers
on my wish list.

281
00:15:53.678 --> 00:15:55.108
Give me number 8.

282
00:16:02.416 --> 00:16:06.486
When I'm 16 I'll have
my own car preferably red.

283
00:16:10.255 --> 00:16:11.383
No way.

284
00:16:11.424 --> 00:16:12.724
Way.

285
00:16:16.192 --> 00:16:17.551
Check it out.

286
00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:21.451
Gosh this is fun.

287
00:16:21.491 --> 00:16:24.290
I can't believe it.
This is my dream car.

288
00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.088
It's all yours sweetie.
Want to drive?

289
00:16:26.128 --> 00:16:27.358
Yes.
No.

290
00:16:27.388 --> 00:16:29.088
Come on. I have my permit.

291
00:16:29.128 --> 00:16:30.298
My dad lets me practice

292
00:16:30.328 --> 00:16:31.797
in the Hasty Mart
parking lot all the time.

293
00:16:31.827 --> 00:16:34.326
Yeah at midnight
when it's empty.

294
00:16:34.366 --> 00:16:36.796
Abby when a total stranger
drives up to you on the street

295
00:16:36.836 --> 00:16:38.864
and offers you a car
you can't just take it.

296
00:16:38.894 --> 00:16:41.704
She's not a total stranger.
You look very familiar.

297
00:16:41.734 --> 00:16:43.633
Well we're not doing this.

298
00:16:43.663 --> 00:16:45.533
Why not?
Yeah why not?

299
00:16:45.573 --> 00:16:48.701
Because...
you don't have a driver's license

300
00:16:48.741 --> 00:16:50.171
until you take the test
after school.

301
00:16:50.201 --> 00:16:53.310
Good point. I'll drive.
You two get in.

302
00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:54.969
What? Not until you
tell us who you are.

303
00:16:55.009 --> 00:16:58.338
I'm Celeste. I'm here to make
Abby's 16 wishes come true.

304
00:16:58.378 --> 00:17:02.547
Oh. Well that explains
pretty much exactly nothing.

305
00:17:02.577 --> 00:17:04.077
Come on Jay.

306
00:17:04.107 --> 00:17:08.046
This is the most wonderful
amazing magical thing

307
00:17:08.076 --> 00:17:09.215
that's ever happened to me.

308
00:17:09.245 --> 00:17:12.643
50 years from now when you're
looking back at your life

309
00:17:12.683 --> 00:17:14.314
don't you want
to be able to say

310
00:17:14.354 --> 00:17:16.412
you had the guts
to get in the car?

311
00:17:19.852 --> 00:17:21.021
I'm going to regret this.

312
00:17:21.051 --> 00:17:24.850
Yes! Get your stuff.
Come on. Get in the car.

313
00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:27.689
All right go go go.

314
00:17:30.828 --> 00:17:34.227
Just so we're clear you're
some kind of magical being

315
00:17:34.257 --> 00:17:35.556
like an elf or a fairy?

316
00:17:35.596 --> 00:17:37.326
Sure. Why not?

317
00:17:37.356 --> 00:17:39.565
You don't sound so sure.
Jay.

318
00:17:39.595 --> 00:17:41.064
You just do birthdays
or other events too?

319
00:17:41.094 --> 00:17:42.524
He babbles when he's nervous.

320
00:17:42.564 --> 00:17:46.063
Why don't you relax Jay
and enjoy the ride?

321
00:17:47.302 --> 00:17:49.233
Hold on.

322
00:17:50.702 --> 00:17:52.401
Yahoo!

323
00:17:52.431 --> 00:17:55.340
Whoa! Mommy!

324
00:17:58.010 --> 00:17:59.409
Whoo!

325
00:18:00.469 --> 00:18:01.908
That was awesome.

326
00:18:01.938 --> 00:18:03.608
Have we landed yet?
What's it look like?

327
00:18:03.638 --> 00:18:05.276
What does what look like?
Her home planet.

328
00:18:05.306 --> 00:18:06.837
Sorry Jay.

329
00:18:06.877 --> 00:18:10.775
The only alien planet you'll be
visiting today is high school.

330
00:18:14.944 --> 00:18:16.712
I already have my license.

331
00:18:16.742 --> 00:18:18.912
My dad has connections
at the DMV.

332
00:18:20.042 --> 00:18:23.181
Yo Logan check out that ride.

333
00:18:28.819 --> 00:18:30.749
Hey Jensen did you
get new wheels too?

334
00:18:30.789 --> 00:18:32.358
Uh...

335
00:18:36.726 --> 00:18:38.926
Yeah. These are my new wheels

336
00:18:38.956 --> 00:18:45.894
which I bought myself for
my birthday which is today.

337
00:18:45.934 --> 00:18:46.934
Cool.

338
00:18:48.463 --> 00:18:50.202
No way this is yours.

339
00:18:50.232 --> 00:18:51.362
What can I say?

340
00:18:51.402 --> 00:18:53.302
I'm a saver
not a spender like you.

341
00:18:53.332 --> 00:18:54.601
Oh man.

342
00:18:54.631 --> 00:18:56.471
I got to make some bank.

343
00:19:08.307 --> 00:19:09.477
Umm...

344
00:19:10.506 --> 00:19:11.545
What are you doing?

345
00:19:11.575 --> 00:19:13.075
Saving you from more
humiliation.

346
00:19:13.115 --> 00:19:14.744
What?
I'm not humiliated.

347
00:19:14.774 --> 00:19:16.414
This is the best birthday ever.

348
00:19:16.444 --> 00:19:17.813
Look. Wish number 15.

349
00:19:17.843 --> 00:19:20.713
When I'm 16 I'll have
the best party ever.

350
00:19:20.743 --> 00:19:22.183
If the candles keep
working like this

351
00:19:22.213 --> 00:19:24.181
my party's going to be sick.

352
00:19:25.381 --> 00:19:26.850
Hey party tonight at my house.

353
00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:28.180
You're all invited.

354
00:19:35.657 --> 00:19:37.258
Come on.

355
00:19:37.288 --> 00:19:38.387
Come on. It's okay.

356
00:19:38.427 --> 00:19:39.957
It's okay.

357
00:19:48.534 --> 00:19:49.593
Want to make some cash?

358
00:19:49.633 --> 00:19:50.833
Yes.

359
00:19:50.863 --> 00:19:52.162
Put these up everywhere.

360
00:19:52.202 --> 00:19:55.331
Meet me at the voting table
after first period.

361
00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:02.669
Okay. You go find
some real clothes to wear.

362
00:20:02.699 --> 00:20:04.869
I'll tell Miss Hackl
you got a late time okay?

363
00:20:04.908 --> 00:20:05.909
Thanks Jay.

364
00:20:13.746 --> 00:20:14.946
Ugh.

365
00:20:14.976 --> 00:20:15.975
Ew.

366
00:20:21.613 --> 00:20:23.112
When I'm 16...

367
00:20:28.521 --> 00:20:31.590
For me? Thank you.

368
00:20:38.927 --> 00:20:39.957
Okay.

369
00:20:43.226 --> 00:20:45.956
Wish number 2. All right.

370
00:20:51.064 --> 00:20:52.133
Okay.

371
00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:03.029
What?

372
00:21:14.076 --> 00:21:15.815
What's going on?

373
00:21:15.845 --> 00:21:17.415
Come on.

374
00:21:21.784 --> 00:21:23.143
Uh Miss Duffy.

375
00:21:23.183 --> 00:21:24.483
Jensen.

376
00:21:26.352 --> 00:21:27.752
I'll take that.

377
00:21:37.449 --> 00:21:40.817
Keep it up Theodore and
you'll be president one day.

378
00:21:40.847 --> 00:21:42.077
You really think so?

379
00:21:42.117 --> 00:21:43.246
Absolutely.

380
00:21:43.286 --> 00:21:44.286
Ohh!

381
00:21:46.915 --> 00:21:48.155
So you can tell the future too?

382
00:21:48.185 --> 00:21:49.915
Oh no. Just gave Ted hope.

383
00:21:49.955 --> 00:21:50.984
Come on in.

384
00:21:54.522 --> 00:21:55.892
So what's up sweetie?

385
00:21:55.922 --> 00:21:57.892
What's up?
You know what's up.

386
00:21:57.922 --> 00:22:00.591
That's why you're here pretending
to be the counselor.

387
00:22:00.621 --> 00:22:02.521
Why didn't that
stupid candle light?

388
00:22:02.561 --> 00:22:04.190
Because of the rules.

389
00:22:04.220 --> 00:22:06.189
The rules?

390
00:22:06.219 --> 00:22:08.819
Oh boy. You don't
get out much do you?

391
00:22:08.859 --> 00:22:10.088
What are you talking about?

392
00:22:10.128 --> 00:22:12.897
The candles are magic
and all magic has rules.

393
00:22:12.927 --> 00:22:15.696
One candle
and one wish per hour.

394
00:22:15.726 --> 00:22:17.925
You lit candle number 1
at 7:58 this morning

395
00:22:17.965 --> 00:22:19.765
and Joey Lockhart showed up.

396
00:22:19.795 --> 00:22:23.094
Then you lit candle number 8
at precisely 8 A.M.

397
00:22:23.134 --> 00:22:26.274
Your wishes were two minutes apart
but within different hours.

398
00:22:26.304 --> 00:22:29.033
Oh. So now I have to wait...

399
00:22:29.073 --> 00:22:31.702
- 27 minutes. - ...
before I make another wish.

400
00:22:31.742 --> 00:22:34.410
Great. You could have printed
that on the box you know.

401
00:22:35.739 --> 00:22:38.238
Any other magic candle rules
I should know about?

402
00:22:38.278 --> 00:22:41.248
Only one but it's a doozy.

403
00:22:41.278 --> 00:22:44.077
The magic in the candles
expires at midnight tonight

404
00:22:44.117 --> 00:22:46.347
so no more wishes after then.

405
00:22:46.387 --> 00:22:49.556
Oh and all the wishes you've
made by then become permanent.

406
00:22:49.586 --> 00:22:51.355
At midnight.
Yeah.

407
00:22:51.385 --> 00:22:54.484
So at midnight that gorgeous
car out there is mine forever?

408
00:22:54.524 --> 00:22:55.653
Absolutely.

409
00:22:55.693 --> 00:22:59.722
And in 26 1/2 minutes I'll have
cuter clothes than Krista Cook.

410
00:22:59.762 --> 00:23:01.621
Yeah.

411
00:23:01.661 --> 00:23:03.731
She really can't stand you.

412
00:23:03.761 --> 00:23:05.390
Oh.

413
00:23:05.430 --> 00:23:06.700
You know about that?

414
00:23:11.599 --> 00:23:13.868
I shouldn't do this but...

415
00:23:16.006 --> 00:23:17.236
Read for yourself.

416
00:23:17.266 --> 00:23:19.865
♪ Oh yeah ♪

417
00:23:19.905 --> 00:23:22.935
Oh no.

418
00:23:22.975 --> 00:23:24.505
I couldn't.

419
00:23:24.535 --> 00:23:26.033
Well maybe just a page or two.

420
00:23:26.073 --> 00:23:28.502
I suggest 10 23 and 37.

421
00:23:29.643 --> 00:23:30.712
Oh.

422
00:23:30.742 --> 00:23:33.810
Be a little more careful where
you light those puppies.

423
00:23:33.840 --> 00:23:35.110
Thanks.

424
00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:37.579
Hmm.

425
00:23:48.556 --> 00:23:49.916
Whoa.

426
00:23:49.956 --> 00:23:51.355
Good stuff?

427
00:23:51.385 --> 00:23:53.924
You have no idea.

428
00:24:03.391 --> 00:24:05.461
Thanks for voting for me.

429
00:24:05.501 --> 00:24:06.901
Krista!

430
00:24:06.931 --> 00:24:10.129
I know you've loathed me
since we were 8 years old

431
00:24:10.169 --> 00:24:12.268
but I didn't know
you've been keeping score.

432
00:24:12.298 --> 00:24:14.468
Where did you get that?

433
00:24:14.498 --> 00:24:15.898
From the Birthday Fairy.

434
00:24:15.938 --> 00:24:18.067
Right. Give it to me.

435
00:24:18.107 --> 00:24:20.836
When we were 10
I had my first sleepover

436
00:24:20.866 --> 00:24:22.266
so you decided to have one too

437
00:24:22.306 --> 00:24:25.005
but you paid everybody
to come to yours.

438
00:24:26.473 --> 00:24:28.773
You have no right
to read that. It's mine.

439
00:24:28.803 --> 00:24:30.643
Well then why
is it all about me?

440
00:24:31.642 --> 00:24:34.771
When we were 12 I entered
the school talent show

441
00:24:34.811 --> 00:24:36.041
with my baton twirling act.

442
00:24:36.081 --> 00:24:38.710
So you entered too
juggli 12 batons.

443
00:24:38.750 --> 00:24:39.780
Sync by Hana.Bean
www.Addic7ed.Com

444
00:24:39.810 --> 00:24:42.279
Every year you' competed with
me and every year you've won.

445
00:24:42.309 --> 00:24:44.149
You've tortured me
since the grade.

446
00:24:44.179 --> 00:24:45.318
Can you just give it a rest?

447
00:24:45.349 --> 00:24:47.117
Don't play innocent with me.

448
00:24:47.147 --> 00:24:48.647
You know what you did.

449
00:24:48.687 --> 00:24:51.787
And for this I'm going to make
sure nobody comes to your party.

450
00:24:51.817 --> 00:24:53.985
Here.

451
00:24:54.015 --> 00:24:55.114
What's this?

452
00:24:55.154 --> 00:24:57.984
It's an invitation to my Sweet
16 birthday party tonight.

453
00:24:58.024 --> 00:24:59.484
Everybody's going to be there.

454
00:24:59.524 --> 00:25:03.791
Now if you'll excuse me I
have some campaigning to do.

455
00:25:03.821 --> 00:25:05.492
Krista you don't
need to campaign.

456
00:25:05.522 --> 00:25:08.691
You're the only name on the
ballot running for president.

457
00:25:08.731 --> 00:25:10.389
Well then I'm sure to win.

458
00:25:10.430 --> 00:25:11.860
Why are you doing this?

459
00:25:11.900 --> 00:25:13.199
You're not even interested
in student government.

460
00:25:13.229 --> 00:25:14.499
And you are?

461
00:25:14.529 --> 00:25:17.758
Well I... I didn't think so.

462
00:25:17.798 --> 00:25:19.198
Ahem.

463
00:25:19.227 --> 00:25:20.697
Hey Krista.

464
00:25:22.066 --> 00:25:24.435
So they said you needed
help with something?

465
00:25:24.465 --> 00:25:25.865
Hand these out for me.

466
00:25:25.895 --> 00:25:27.234
Sure.

467
00:25:27.264 --> 00:25:28.235
Thanks.

468
00:25:33.033 --> 00:25:35.172
She's doing it.
She's ruining my birthday.

469
00:25:35.202 --> 00:25:36.271
Again.

470
00:25:36.301 --> 00:25:39.371
Just don't let her get to you.

471
00:25:39.401 --> 00:25:40.941
You're right Jay.

472
00:25:40.971 --> 00:25:43.610
I'm going to put an end
to her reign of terror.

473
00:25:45.008 --> 00:25:48.408
Right about now.

474
00:26:06.492 --> 00:26:08.231
List. Hurry.

475
00:26:20.738 --> 00:26:24.667
When I'm 16 I'll have
the cutest clothes in school.

476
00:26:27.935 --> 00:26:29.935
Hi-hi.

477
00:26:29.975 --> 00:26:32.634
Celeste it's beautiful.

478
00:26:32.673 --> 00:26:33.804
I know right?

479
00:26:33.843 --> 00:26:35.973
I've been waiting for you
to make this wish.

480
00:26:36.003 --> 00:26:38.972
I just love shopping
especially when it's free.

481
00:26:39.012 --> 00:26:40.741
I don't even know
where to start.

482
00:26:40.781 --> 00:26:42.181
That's what I'm here for.

483
00:26:42.211 --> 00:26:44.740
Now close your eyes
and let me work my magic.

484
00:26:46.249 --> 00:26:49.448
Ever since the third grade
whatever I did Krista did better.

485
00:26:49.478 --> 00:26:52.847
She's never satisfied unless
she's winning and I'm losing.

486
00:26:52.887 --> 00:26:56.586
But today I decided she's t going
to make me miserable anymore.

487
00:26:58.015 --> 00:27:02.784
I have a plan and this
wish it's the first part.

488
00:27:02.824 --> 00:27:04.353
Would you say
Krista Cook always has

489
00:27:04.393 --> 00:27:05.754
the cutest clothes in school?

490
00:27:05.794 --> 00:27:07.762
And shoes and handbags.

491
00:27:09.221 --> 00:27:10.992
Not anymore.

492
00:27:26.805 --> 00:27:29.205
That top is not an original
you-know-who is it?

493
00:27:29.235 --> 00:27:31.175
It is.

494
00:27:31.205 --> 00:27:32.344
Shut up.

495
00:27:32.374 --> 00:27:34.404
Oh those shoes
are so to die for.

496
00:27:34.444 --> 00:27:36.243
I hate you.

497
00:27:36.273 --> 00:27:37.543
Want to have lunch near us?

498
00:27:37.573 --> 00:27:38.742
Sure.

499
00:27:38.782 --> 00:27:41.841
Yay. I totally just want to
sit next to that handbag.

500
00:27:41.881 --> 00:27:43.910
You mean this handbag?

501
00:27:45.881 --> 00:27:49.379
I got it for my birthday last year.

502
00:27:49.419 --> 00:27:50.979
You're not all that Jensen.

503
00:27:55.716 --> 00:27:56.886
Yoo-hoo Abby!

504
00:27:57.986 --> 00:27:59.686
I'm so sorry.

505
00:27:59.726 --> 00:28:01.285
Give me that old thing.

506
00:28:01.325 --> 00:28:05.493
This one's so hot it
hasn't even come out yet.

507
00:28:05.523 --> 00:28:07.223
Thank you so much.

508
00:28:07.263 --> 00:28:09.823
I'll just ship you
the rest of the collection

509
00:28:09.863 --> 00:28:11.562
when the infestation's over.

510
00:28:11.592 --> 00:28:13.061
Auf Wiedersehen.

511
00:28:27.836 --> 00:28:30.705
I know what you're doing
and it's not going to work.

512
00:28:32.175 --> 00:28:35.035
I'm just trying to have the best
birthday of my entire life.

513
00:28:35.074 --> 00:28:37.574
Well good luck with that
because it's not over yet.

514
00:28:59.685 --> 00:29:02.655
All right everybody.
On the track in five.

515
00:29:02.685 --> 00:29:04.714
Late again Jensen.

516
00:29:06.754 --> 00:29:09.153
Yes Miss Duffy I am late.

517
00:29:09.183 --> 00:29:12.092
I had to go back to my locker
for this.

518
00:29:13.152 --> 00:29:14.991
I see.

519
00:29:15.021 --> 00:29:16.461
That's still no excuse
for tardiness

520
00:29:16.491 --> 00:29:18.960
but that is a beautiful bag.

521
00:29:20.030 --> 00:29:21.400
It's for you.

522
00:29:21.429 --> 00:29:23.458
Me?
Mm-hmm.

523
00:29:23.498 --> 00:29:25.169
I was saving it
for your Christmas present

524
00:29:25.199 --> 00:29:29.897
but look it matches
your track suit perfectly.

525
00:29:29.937 --> 00:29:31.407
Ha ha! It actually does.

526
00:29:31.436 --> 00:29:32.335
Happy Monday.

527
00:29:32.365 --> 00:29:34.604
Well Happy Monday to me.

528
00:29:34.634 --> 00:29:38.804
Well ladies what do you say
instead of running killer laps

529
00:29:38.844 --> 00:29:41.233
we all have a nice friendly
game of volleyball?

530
00:29:42.903 --> 00:29:43.972
Way to go Abby.

531
00:29:57.418 --> 00:29:58.517
Sync by Hana.Bean
www.Addic7ed.Com

532
00:30:06.684 --> 00:30:08.484
Come on. We need her.

533
00:30:08.524 --> 00:30:09.623
Jensen!

534
00:30:09.653 --> 00:30:11.654
Get out here!

535
00:30:15.292 --> 00:30:20.191
When I'm 16 I'll beat Krista
at something anything.

536
00:30:20.231 --> 00:30:21.960
Everything.

537
00:30:27.068 --> 00:30:28.767
Sync by Hana.Bean
www.Addic7ed.Com

538
00:30:44.742 --> 00:30:46.413
Play ball!

539
00:30:54.479 --> 00:30:56.278
You sure you're ready for this?

540
00:30:56.318 --> 00:30:57.949
Why shouldn't I be sure?

541
00:30:57.979 --> 00:31:00.288
Because you're the least
athletic person I know.

542
00:31:00.318 --> 00:31:03.117
Not anymore.
I got the birthday mojo.

543
00:31:03.147 --> 00:31:04.785
Duck!

544
00:31:04.815 --> 00:31:06.656
1-zip.

545
00:31:06.686 --> 00:31:08.985
You tried to hit me.

546
00:31:09.025 --> 00:31:12.393
It's called spiking.
It's how you win.

547
00:31:13.522 --> 00:31:15.263
Play ball!

548
00:31:44.244 --> 00:31:46.643
MVP! MVP!

549
00:31:46.673 --> 00:31:48.541
Hey are you all right?

550
00:31:48.571 --> 00:31:50.812
I'm going
to call the nurse okay?

551
00:31:50.842 --> 00:31:51.941
Stay here.

552
00:31:51.981 --> 00:31:56.179
MVP! MVP! MVP!

553
00:32:04.047 --> 00:32:05.687
Oh well look who's awake.

554
00:32:07.816 --> 00:32:08.914
How are you feeling?

555
00:32:08.954 --> 00:32:10.455
I'm fine.

556
00:32:10.485 --> 00:32:12.194
I had a weird nightmare.

557
00:32:12.224 --> 00:32:15.623
Oh honey that was real.
Abby Jensen creamed you.

558
00:32:15.663 --> 00:32:17.522
Oh and you're wanted
in the principal's office.

559
00:32:25.730 --> 00:32:26.700
Run along.

560
00:32:30.469 --> 00:32:34.338
Yeah that's so true.
That's so true.

561
00:32:35.937 --> 00:32:37.336
Makes my day.
Yeah.

562
00:32:37.376 --> 00:32:39.075
You wanted to see me
Mr. Smith?

563
00:32:39.105 --> 00:32:41.374
Yeah. Yeah.

564
00:32:41.414 --> 00:32:45.143
Ms. Cook
the election's over.

565
00:32:45.183 --> 00:32:48.183
How can it be over?
A lot of people haven't voted yet.

566
00:32:49.313 --> 00:32:53.621
Actually we had a 100% voter turnout.

567
00:32:55.750 --> 00:32:57.420
Whoop! Ooh!

568
00:32:57.460 --> 00:32:58.689
What's going on here?

569
00:33:03.598 --> 00:33:08.396
Good morning students!

570
00:33:08.426 --> 00:33:10.395
I'm very pleased to announce

571
00:33:10.435 --> 00:33:14.064
the winner of the most votes
for the Student Body President

572
00:33:14.104 --> 00:33:18.134
is Abby Jensen!

573
00:33:20.472 --> 00:33:21.972
Yes!

574
00:33:23.342 --> 00:33:25.811
I just want to thank
everyone who voted for me

575
00:33:25.841 --> 00:33:27.241
and made this dream possible.

576
00:33:27.270 --> 00:33:29.570
No. It's not possible.

577
00:33:29.610 --> 00:33:31.538
Her name isn't
even on the ballots!

578
00:33:33.638 --> 00:33:37.277
Let... go.

579
00:33:41.646 --> 00:33:43.415
That is all.

580
00:33:43.445 --> 00:33:45.214
Whoa. Wow.
You all right?

581
00:33:45.244 --> 00:33:46.754
Abby was a write-in.

582
00:33:53.621 --> 00:33:55.752
Better luck next time Krista.

583
00:34:21.832 --> 00:34:22.901
Ha!

584
00:34:22.931 --> 00:34:24.902
I finally beat Krista Cook.

585
00:34:24.932 --> 00:34:26.171
Had a little help.

586
00:34:26.201 --> 00:34:28.500
I know. Isn't it amazing?

587
00:34:28.530 --> 00:34:30.330
This day just keeps
getting better and better.

588
00:34:30.370 --> 00:34:31.599
Yeah for you.

589
00:34:31.639 --> 00:34:32.639
I know right?

590
00:34:32.669 --> 00:34:34.398
♪ Oi ♪

591
00:34:34.438 --> 00:34:35.568
♪ Java ♪

592
00:34:35.608 --> 00:34:36.608
♪ Oi ♪

593
00:34:36.638 --> 00:34:37.637
Can we just do this experiment?

594
00:34:37.667 --> 00:34:39.037
We both need extra credit.

595
00:34:39.077 --> 00:34:40.236
Nah.

596
00:34:40.276 --> 00:34:43.205
I'll just give the teacher some
strappy sandals and a pashmina.

597
00:34:43.246 --> 00:34:46.174
No. Just give it a rest.

598
00:34:46.204 --> 00:34:48.345
What's wrong with you?

599
00:34:48.375 --> 00:34:49.973
I don't know.
This whole wish thing.

600
00:34:50.013 --> 00:34:51.673
You're changing too fast Abby.

601
00:34:51.712 --> 00:34:53.012
I can't keep up.

602
00:34:53.042 --> 00:34:54.342
What do you mean?

603
00:34:54.382 --> 00:34:57.152
You've always been
allergic to volunteer work.

604
00:34:57.182 --> 00:34:59.280
And now all of a sudden
you're Student Body President?

605
00:34:59.310 --> 00:35:00.549
What can I say?

606
00:35:00.579 --> 00:35:03.549
The people spoke
and they wanted me.

607
00:35:03.579 --> 00:35:07.288
The candles spoke and you have no
idea what you just wished for.

608
00:35:07.318 --> 00:35:08.518
Yes I do.

609
00:35:08.558 --> 00:35:11.986
Being president
is like an honor.

610
00:35:12.016 --> 00:35:14.656
Being president is
an important job Abby.

611
00:35:14.686 --> 00:35:16.625
It should do to someone
who really wants it.

612
00:35:16.655 --> 00:35:19.624
Oh like who? Like Krista?

613
00:35:19.654 --> 00:35:20.654
No.

614
00:35:21.863 --> 00:35:24.122
Well I'm sure
I'll do just fine.

615
00:35:24.162 --> 00:35:26.162
I'll have you to help me.

616
00:35:26.192 --> 00:35:28.462
Come on.
You can't be mad at me.

617
00:35:28.492 --> 00:35:29.590
Why not?

618
00:35:29.631 --> 00:35:31.700
Because it's my birthday.

619
00:35:33.670 --> 00:35:35.598
Because we're best friends.

620
00:35:38.568 --> 00:35:43.867
Because I'm Student Body President
and I get free lunch. Ta-da!

621
00:35:44.976 --> 00:35:46.006
No way.

622
00:35:46.036 --> 00:35:48.505
Way way. Every day.

623
00:35:48.545 --> 00:35:51.344
Now hand over
your goofy glasses

624
00:35:51.374 --> 00:35:54.412
and let your commander in chief
buy you a sandwich.

625
00:35:55.841 --> 00:35:56.912
What kind of sandwich?

626
00:35:56.951 --> 00:35:59.251
Any kind you want.

627
00:36:05.659 --> 00:36:07.119
Come on.

628
00:36:07.159 --> 00:36:08.988
There she is!

629
00:36:10.557 --> 00:36:13.796
You see? Ha ha.
They love me.

630
00:36:13.826 --> 00:36:15.496
What have you done now?

631
00:36:15.526 --> 00:36:17.695
Wish number 10.

632
00:36:18.696 --> 00:36:21.764
I looked in the mirror and I
was tired of being invisible.

633
00:36:21.794 --> 00:36:24.463
When I'm 16 I'll be popular.

634
00:36:24.493 --> 00:36:26.033
Oh hi Joey.

635
00:36:26.063 --> 00:36:28.401
Abby smile!

636
00:36:28.431 --> 00:36:30.362
Sure I'll sign it.

637
00:36:33.470 --> 00:36:35.000
I loved that wish.

638
00:36:35.030 --> 00:36:36.500
Right.

639
00:36:42.067 --> 00:36:43.506
Okay people make a hole!

640
00:36:43.536 --> 00:36:44.666
Here she comes!

641
00:36:44.706 --> 00:36:45.736
Back up. Come on.

642
00:36:45.776 --> 00:36:47.336
Move your hair.
Thank you. Okay.

643
00:36:47.376 --> 00:36:48.534
Peeps.

644
00:36:51.844 --> 00:36:53.474
And I don't have to do a thing.

645
00:36:53.514 --> 00:36:54.713
Just show up.

646
00:36:54.743 --> 00:36:56.843
They're planning
your birthday party.

647
00:36:56.882 --> 00:36:58.312
Mm-hmm.

648
00:37:01.011 --> 00:37:02.910
Their dads
are business partners.

649
00:37:02.950 --> 00:37:04.951
Apparently
they own half of Vegas.

650
00:37:04.981 --> 00:37:06.849
They're throwing my party
at one of their hotels.

651
00:37:08.049 --> 00:37:11.777
Not to rain on your birthday
parade Abs but Vegas?

652
00:37:11.817 --> 00:37:14.118
That's not really your style.

653
00:37:14.148 --> 00:37:15.716
And your basement is?

654
00:37:15.746 --> 00:37:17.546
Hey I have foosball.

655
00:37:17.586 --> 00:37:19.815
Good point.

656
00:37:19.855 --> 00:37:23.353
Look this is my one and only
Sweet 16 birthday party.

657
00:37:23.383 --> 00:37:25.893
I... I want it to be
spectacular.

658
00:37:28.462 --> 00:37:30.002
I don't have anything to wear.

659
00:37:30.032 --> 00:37:31.871
Well we both have
a free period right now.

660
00:37:31.901 --> 00:37:33.801
Let's go buy you a dress.

661
00:37:33.841 --> 00:37:37.699
We can't. The wasps are holding
my party money hostage.

662
00:37:37.739 --> 00:37:38.909
I'll supply you the cash.

663
00:37:38.939 --> 00:37:40.568
You'd do that?

664
00:37:40.608 --> 00:37:41.708
Sure.

665
00:37:41.738 --> 00:37:44.007
Jay you're the best.

666
00:37:58.382 --> 00:38:00.213
We can't go.

667
00:38:00.243 --> 00:38:02.451
I don't have my license yet.

668
00:38:05.621 --> 00:38:08.120
A reading from the Wish List
of Abigail Jensen.

669
00:38:08.150 --> 00:38:11.088
Wish number 7... When I'm 16...

670
00:38:36.800 --> 00:38:39.210
Abigail Louise Jensen?

671
00:38:39.240 --> 00:38:41.680
Yes.

672
00:38:41.709 --> 00:38:43.708
This is highly unusual.

673
00:38:50.177 --> 00:38:53.385
My driver's license!

674
00:38:53.415 --> 00:38:55.585
And there ya go.

675
00:38:55.615 --> 00:38:57.313
Thank you so much!

676
00:39:04.322 --> 00:39:05.591
Oh lighten up Harry.

677
00:39:05.621 --> 00:39:08.460
You needed to get out of
that cubicle anyway.

678
00:39:08.490 --> 00:39:10.230
But we really don't
do this kind of thing.

679
00:39:10.260 --> 00:39:11.489
I know.

680
00:39:11.529 --> 00:39:13.928
But wasn't it fun?

681
00:39:13.958 --> 00:39:16.228
My cubicle was fun.

682
00:39:19.497 --> 00:39:21.296
♪ My baby ♪

683
00:39:21.336 --> 00:39:22.966
♪ Goin' for a ride ♪

684
00:39:31.943 --> 00:39:34.871
♪ Ride and ride and ride ♪

685
00:39:34.911 --> 00:39:36.942
♪ Ride and ride and ride... ♪

686
00:39:42.579 --> 00:39:44.419
Jay?
Yes Abs.

687
00:39:44.449 --> 00:39:47.348
This is now officially
the best 16th birthday

688
00:39:47.388 --> 00:39:50.687
in the history
of 16th birthdays.

689
00:39:53.216 --> 00:39:55.155
Abby you can't afford
a hanger here.

690
00:39:55.185 --> 00:39:56.485
Not true.

691
00:39:56.525 --> 00:39:58.024
Since I don't have
to pay for my own party

692
00:39:58.054 --> 00:40:00.583
I'm spending every penny I
saved on the perfect dress.

693
00:40:02.853 --> 00:40:03.852
Come on!

694
00:40:11.861 --> 00:40:13.689
What do you think?
It's nice.

695
00:40:13.729 --> 00:40:16.468
No. Too disco.

696
00:40:26.036 --> 00:40:28.005
What about this one?

697
00:40:28.035 --> 00:40:32.343
You're... It's beautiful.

698
00:40:32.373 --> 00:40:34.913
But do you think Logan
will like it?

699
00:40:34.943 --> 00:40:36.472
How should I know?

700
00:40:36.511 --> 00:40:37.582
Touchy.

701
00:40:37.612 --> 00:40:39.210
Why don't you just light
No. 16 right now

702
00:40:39.241 --> 00:40:40.641
and make the stupid wish?

703
00:40:40.681 --> 00:40:42.310
Poof.
Logan Buchanan is yours.

704
00:40:42.350 --> 00:40:43.280
It doesn't work that way.

705
00:40:43.310 --> 00:40:44.579
Uh yes it does.

706
00:40:44.619 --> 00:40:46.279
It's worked that way all day.

707
00:40:46.319 --> 00:40:48.448
I want Logan to like me for me

708
00:40:48.478 --> 00:40:52.417
not because I put some magic
birthday spell on him.

709
00:40:52.447 --> 00:40:53.816
I'm trying this on.

710
00:40:56.685 --> 00:40:57.985
And these.

711
00:41:18.529 --> 00:41:21.897
I'll take these.

712
00:41:21.927 --> 00:41:23.867
I really feel for you.

713
00:41:23.897 --> 00:41:27.196
Wasting your time on kids
like that.

714
00:41:27.236 --> 00:41:28.435
A customer's a customer.

715
00:41:28.465 --> 00:41:30.535
Oh trust me.

716
00:41:30.564 --> 00:41:34.263
They won't be buying anything.

717
00:41:34.303 --> 00:41:36.973
Look Jay.
It's perfect isn't it?

718
00:41:37.003 --> 00:41:38.572
Sure.

719
00:41:38.602 --> 00:41:41.641
Well I love it and I think
Logan's going to love it too.

720
00:41:41.671 --> 00:41:43.341
Good. Sold.

721
00:41:43.371 --> 00:41:45.209
Can we go now?

722
00:41:45.239 --> 00:41:47.939
Don't be so grumpy.

723
00:41:47.979 --> 00:41:49.078
I'm sorry.

724
00:41:49.108 --> 00:41:51.178
This is a store
not a playground.

725
00:41:51.218 --> 00:41:52.847
Exactly.

726
00:41:52.887 --> 00:41:53.946
I like this one.

727
00:41:53.986 --> 00:41:55.216
I'm sure you do.

728
00:41:55.256 --> 00:41:57.456
Why don't you kids just come
back with your parents?

729
00:41:57.486 --> 00:41:59.755
We're not kids. I'm 16.

730
00:41:59.785 --> 00:42:01.125
Congratulations.

731
00:42:01.155 --> 00:42:02.185
Now give me the dress.

732
00:42:02.225 --> 00:42:04.123
No we're buying it!

733
00:42:04.153 --> 00:42:06.163
Jay show her your money.

734
00:42:09.992 --> 00:42:13.461
My wallet... You out.

735
00:42:13.501 --> 00:42:15.600
Hey!
You can't do that!

736
00:42:15.630 --> 00:42:17.070
Watch me.

737
00:42:18.869 --> 00:42:19.899
But we're customers!

738
00:42:19.939 --> 00:42:21.298
No you're children.

739
00:42:21.338 --> 00:42:23.967
Get that dress off now.

740
00:42:42.682 --> 00:42:44.951
Wish number 9...

741
00:42:56.827 --> 00:43:01.665
When I'm 16 people will
stop treating me like a kid.

742
00:43:13.871 --> 00:43:16.370
When I'm 16 people will stop
treating me like a kid.

743
00:43:31.016 --> 00:43:34.785
Um excuse me where's my friend?

744
00:43:34.815 --> 00:43:36.584
There was a boy here

745
00:43:36.614 --> 00:43:39.353
but he left with a girl in
the cutest little yellow car...

746
00:43:39.383 --> 00:43:42.012
Wait. He left with Krista?

747
00:43:42.051 --> 00:43:43.722
It appears so.

748
00:43:43.752 --> 00:43:46.791
Turn around.

749
00:43:46.821 --> 00:43:48.250
That outfit is all wrong.

750
00:43:48.290 --> 00:43:49.920
It's far too young for you.

751
00:43:49.960 --> 00:43:51.719
And suddenly really tight.

752
00:43:51.759 --> 00:43:55.388
Let's get you into something
more age appropriate.

753
00:43:55.428 --> 00:43:58.827
Let's try these.

754
00:43:58.857 --> 00:44:01.596
But I don't have any money.

755
00:44:01.626 --> 00:44:05.095
Oh we'll just put them
on your charge account.

756
00:44:05.135 --> 00:44:09.233
I have a charge account?

757
00:44:09.263 --> 00:44:10.932
Is everything all right
Miss Jensen?

758
00:44:10.962 --> 00:44:12.202
Oh yeah.

759
00:44:12.232 --> 00:44:16.502
Everything is just fine.

760
00:44:16.541 --> 00:44:20.170
♪ It's a picture perfect world ♪

761
00:44:20.210 --> 00:44:23.179
♪ A picture perfect world ♪

762
00:44:25.059 --> 00:44:28.128
♪ This time we're doing it our way ♪

763
00:44:28.167 --> 00:44:29.397
Thank you so much.

764
00:44:29.427 --> 00:44:31.666
♪ We've got a new perspective ♪

765
00:44:31.696 --> 00:44:34.765
♪ It's time for us to make the grade ♪

766
00:44:34.805 --> 00:44:36.805
♪ Head in a new direction ♪

767
00:44:36.835 --> 00:44:40.573
♪ So it's a picture perfect
world we live in ♪

768
00:44:40.603 --> 00:44:42.333
♪ Starting today ♪

769
00:44:42.373 --> 00:44:46.041
♪ It's a picture perfect world
we're given ♪

770
00:44:46.071 --> 00:44:48.911
♪ Make no mistake ♪

771
00:44:48.941 --> 00:44:50.171
♪ The sun's in the sky ♪

772
00:44:55.249 --> 00:44:58.377
♪ It's a picture perfect world ♪

773
00:44:59.647 --> 00:45:01.677
Sorry Miss Duffy.

774
00:45:01.717 --> 00:45:04.475
Do we know each other?

775
00:45:04.515 --> 00:45:06.044
Yeah.

776
00:45:06.084 --> 00:45:07.785
Ah you're the new
substitute teacher

777
00:45:07.815 --> 00:45:10.714
which means I don't have to
babysit those little monsters.

778
00:45:10.754 --> 00:45:12.853
They're all yours.

779
00:45:30.897 --> 00:45:32.826
Psssst!

780
00:45:46.413 --> 00:45:47.842
Psssst! Jay!

781
00:45:54.110 --> 00:45:56.348
I'll be right back.

782
00:45:56.379 --> 00:45:57.949
Oh great.

783
00:45:57.979 --> 00:45:59.917
Leave me to wrangle
the Blob all alone.

784
00:46:01.547 --> 00:46:03.187
Okay go.

785
00:46:10.384 --> 00:46:11.524
Yes?

786
00:46:11.554 --> 00:46:12.624
Get out here!

787
00:46:15.393 --> 00:46:16.692
What's wrong with you?

788
00:46:16.722 --> 00:46:18.092
Excuse me?

789
00:46:18.122 --> 00:46:20.931
You left me stranded
on my birthday.

790
00:46:20.961 --> 00:46:22.961
What kind of a best friend
does that?

791
00:46:23.001 --> 00:46:25.400
Best friend?
What are you talking about?

792
00:46:25.430 --> 00:46:27.099
Oh hi.
My name is Abby Jensen.

793
00:46:27.129 --> 00:46:29.069
Have we met?

794
00:46:29.099 --> 00:46:31.598
Yeah.
A long time ago I think.

795
00:46:31.638 --> 00:46:32.597
Shut up.

796
00:46:32.637 --> 00:46:34.237
Stop it.

797
00:46:34.267 --> 00:46:35.206
I'm not your best friend.

798
00:46:35.237 --> 00:46:40.475
I'm a sophomore.
You're a... woman.

799
00:46:40.505 --> 00:46:43.104
Thank you but I'm just
four months older than you.

800
00:46:43.144 --> 00:46:45.142
Yeah in dog years.

801
00:46:45.172 --> 00:46:47.813
Listen I'm in the middle of
an important experiment...

802
00:46:47.843 --> 00:46:49.782
And I'm in the middle of
an important birthday!

803
00:46:49.812 --> 00:46:51.151
I'm sorry. I gotta go.

804
00:46:51.181 --> 00:46:54.880
No wait... Let go.

805
00:46:59.349 --> 00:47:00.319
Jay Kepler!

806
00:47:00.359 --> 00:47:02.418
You're the worst
best friend ever!

807
00:47:04.387 --> 00:47:05.457
I don't understand.

808
00:47:05.487 --> 00:47:07.486
Am I being expelled?

809
00:47:07.526 --> 00:47:10.795
I'm sure they'll
explain everything.

810
00:47:10.825 --> 00:47:12.594
Mom? Dad?

811
00:47:12.624 --> 00:47:14.324
What's the truck for?

812
00:47:14.364 --> 00:47:16.333
Are we moving?

813
00:47:16.363 --> 00:47:17.632
Just come with us.

814
00:47:17.662 --> 00:47:19.802
Not until somebody tells me
what's going on?

815
00:47:22.731 --> 00:47:25.100
Abby you can't go to
high school anymore.

816
00:47:25.140 --> 00:47:26.499
What? Why not?

817
00:47:26.539 --> 00:47:27.669
Because it's time you grow up.

818
00:47:27.709 --> 00:47:28.968
Bob.
What?

819
00:47:29.008 --> 00:47:30.338
Sweetheart while the
house is being fumigated

820
00:47:30.379 --> 00:47:31.678
there just really
isn't room for you.

821
00:47:31.708 --> 00:47:34.677
So your dad and I were talking...
We found you an apartment...

822
00:47:34.707 --> 00:47:35.977
A what?

823
00:47:36.007 --> 00:47:37.117
An apartment.

824
00:47:37.147 --> 00:47:38.846
To live in.

825
00:47:38.876 --> 00:47:40.515
By myself?

826
00:47:53.251 --> 00:47:54.691
It's a very safe neighborhood.

827
00:47:54.721 --> 00:47:55.860
Is that what you call it?

828
00:47:55.890 --> 00:47:57.290
I call it pricey.

829
00:47:57.320 --> 00:47:59.189
Your dad and I paid
the security deposit

830
00:47:59.230 --> 00:48:01.959
but the first month's rent
is your responsibility.

831
00:48:08.467 --> 00:48:11.096
Okay I'll get the last load.

832
00:48:11.136 --> 00:48:12.465
You're going to need
a full-time job.

833
00:48:12.495 --> 00:48:13.765
I circled some good ones...

834
00:48:13.805 --> 00:48:16.703
What? No. I can't go
to school and have a job.

835
00:48:16.733 --> 00:48:19.232
Oh well if you're ready
for college... Bob!

836
00:48:19.273 --> 00:48:20.503
Yeah!

837
00:48:20.543 --> 00:48:21.542
She wants to go to college!

838
00:48:21.572 --> 00:48:22.971
No not yet!

839
00:48:23.001 --> 00:48:23.942
Never mind.

840
00:48:23.972 --> 00:48:25.041
Okay.

841
00:48:25.071 --> 00:48:26.671
Mom I'm just a kid!

842
00:48:26.711 --> 00:48:28.370
I can't live here by myself!

843
00:48:28.410 --> 00:48:29.680
Abby don't be so dramatic.

844
00:48:29.710 --> 00:48:31.880
Lots of girls your age
have their own apartments.

845
00:48:31.909 --> 00:48:34.208
I moved out when I was 18.

846
00:48:34.248 --> 00:48:35.408
But I'm not 18.

847
00:48:35.448 --> 00:48:36.577
No you're 21.

848
00:48:36.617 --> 00:48:37.577
22 today.

849
00:48:37.617 --> 00:48:39.417
Happy Birthday sweetheart.

850
00:48:39.447 --> 00:48:41.186
What are you talking about?

851
00:48:41.216 --> 00:48:42.515
Let's go Sue.

852
00:48:42.555 --> 00:48:44.015
No! Don't go!

853
00:48:44.055 --> 00:48:47.125
Just remember we did this out
of love... Yeah tough love.

854
00:48:47.155 --> 00:48:49.183
Bob!

855
00:48:49.223 --> 00:48:50.653
You'll be fine Pumpkin.

856
00:48:50.693 --> 00:48:52.662
Dad Dad...

857
00:48:55.032 --> 00:49:01.969
Mom...
Come and visit anytime.

858
00:49:01.999 --> 00:49:03.269
Except Wednesdays.

859
00:49:03.299 --> 00:49:05.537
Wednesday is our bowling night.

860
00:49:15.905 --> 00:49:17.744
High school memories?

861
00:49:45.156 --> 00:49:47.125
No.

862
00:49:47.155 --> 00:49:48.194
When I'm 16...

863
00:49:52.563 --> 00:49:56.492
Let's get you into something
more age-appropriate.

864
00:49:56.532 --> 00:49:57.791
You're the new substitute
teacher.

865
00:49:57.831 --> 00:49:59.531
Stop it!
I'm not your best friend.

866
00:49:59.561 --> 00:50:00.400
I'm a sophomore.

867
00:50:00.430 --> 00:50:03.359
You're a...
woman.

868
00:50:03.399 --> 00:50:04.429
No you're 21.

869
00:50:04.469 --> 00:50:06.128
22 today.

870
00:50:06.168 --> 00:50:08.867
Happy Birthday sweetheart.

871
00:50:08.897 --> 00:50:10.067
Oh no.

872
00:50:10.097 --> 00:50:11.337
No no no.

873
00:50:11.367 --> 00:50:13.507
This isn't what I wanted!

874
00:50:22.144 --> 00:50:24.472
Celeste!

875
00:50:24.512 --> 00:50:27.971
Celeste I need to talk to you!

876
00:50:28.011 --> 00:50:30.181
Right now!

877
00:50:33.450 --> 00:50:34.980
The list.

878
00:50:37.749 --> 00:50:41.547
There's gotta be a wish.

879
00:50:41.587 --> 00:50:44.286
That's it! Wish number 3.

880
00:50:44.316 --> 00:50:46.146
That should do it.

881
00:50:50.054 --> 00:50:54.724
When I'm 16 I'll decorate
my room the way I want.

882
00:50:59.021 --> 00:51:00.221
Yoo-hoo!

883
00:51:01.690 --> 00:51:02.930
Decorator's Delight!

884
00:51:02.960 --> 00:51:06.160
Celeste!
I'm so glad you're here... Me too.

885
00:51:06.200 --> 00:51:08.098
Okay. Nice.

886
00:51:08.128 --> 00:51:10.168
Lots of potential.

887
00:51:10.198 --> 00:51:11.867
I need your help.
You sure do.

888
00:51:11.897 --> 00:51:14.396
Maybe some wallpaper...
No no wallpaper.

889
00:51:14.436 --> 00:51:15.895
Paint then.

890
00:51:15.935 --> 00:51:16.895
Let's look at some samples.

891
00:51:16.935 --> 00:51:18.036
No listen to me.

892
00:51:18.066 --> 00:51:19.765
Your magic candles
made a mistake.

893
00:51:19.805 --> 00:51:20.934
Candles don't make mistakes.

894
00:51:20.964 --> 00:51:22.604
People do.

895
00:51:22.634 --> 00:51:25.503
I made a wish but it
wasn't really my wish.

896
00:51:25.533 --> 00:51:27.303
How about some curtains?

897
00:51:27.343 --> 00:51:28.441
No!

898
00:51:28.471 --> 00:51:29.542
Oo bad decision.

899
00:51:29.572 --> 00:51:30.571
You need privacy.

900
00:51:30.601 --> 00:51:31.401
You're alone.

901
00:51:31.441 --> 00:51:33.610
You're a woman... No I'm not!

902
00:51:33.640 --> 00:51:34.570
I'm not a woman!

903
00:51:34.610 --> 00:51:35.940
I'm 16 years old!

904
00:51:35.980 --> 00:51:40.778
I made a wish... wish number 9.

905
00:51:40.808 --> 00:51:42.047
I didn't want to be an adult!

906
00:51:42.077 --> 00:51:44.547
I just wanted to be
treated like one!

907
00:51:44.577 --> 00:51:46.117
The candles have
their own logic.

908
00:51:46.147 --> 00:51:47.387
They don't always give you
what you want.

909
00:51:47.417 --> 00:51:48.916
Sometimes they give you
what you need.

910
00:51:48.946 --> 00:51:51.884
And sweetie
you need drapes pronto.

911
00:51:51.914 --> 00:51:53.854
I don't need drapes!

912
00:51:53.884 --> 00:51:55.553
I need my life back!

913
00:51:55.583 --> 00:51:56.752
I just wished away my friends

914
00:51:56.782 --> 00:51:59.392
my Sweet 16 party
my senior prom...

915
00:52:01.262 --> 00:52:03.921
I missed graduation!

916
00:52:03.961 --> 00:52:05.690
I need to take that wish back!

917
00:52:05.730 --> 00:52:08.689
Oh sweetie.

918
00:52:08.729 --> 00:52:10.829
I'm afraid that's not possible.

919
00:52:10.859 --> 00:52:13.398
The candles and your
wishes go together.

920
00:52:13.428 --> 00:52:16.027
Since there's no do-over
wish on your list...

921
00:52:16.066 --> 00:52:19.566
I'm afraid when midnight
comes this is your life.

922
00:52:21.865 --> 00:52:22.864
But...

923
00:52:25.534 --> 00:52:27.133
Decorator's Delight.

924
00:52:27.173 --> 00:52:28.873
Uh-huh.

925
00:52:28.903 --> 00:52:30.272
On my way.

926
00:52:30.302 --> 00:52:31.373
Slipcover emergency.

927
00:52:31.403 --> 00:52:32.572
Gotta run.

928
00:52:32.602 --> 00:52:35.370
What? No no no!

929
00:52:35.410 --> 00:52:37.610
Wait!

930
00:52:37.640 --> 00:52:41.549
Celeste Celeste...

931
00:52:47.116 --> 00:52:48.486
You tryin' to run out
on the rent?

932
00:52:48.516 --> 00:52:50.086
No!
Good.

933
00:52:50.116 --> 00:52:51.786
First month is due
in three days.

934
00:52:51.816 --> 00:52:53.185
Pay up or move out.

935
00:52:57.024 --> 00:52:58.722
Move out.

936
00:53:01.622 --> 00:53:03.521
Move out.

937
00:53:11.029 --> 00:53:12.358
Stupid wishes!

938
00:53:12.398 --> 00:53:14.898
Why did I ever write you down!

939
00:53:21.706 --> 00:53:23.905
I'll just change one.

940
00:53:50.846 --> 00:53:52.016
Ha!

941
00:53:52.056 --> 00:53:53.515
Gotcha!

942
00:54:03.492 --> 00:54:06.061
I hate sushi and I always will!

943
00:54:13.798 --> 00:54:15.669
Hey...

944
00:54:16.968 --> 00:54:20.967
What about you
Wish No. 14?

945
00:54:21.007 --> 00:54:22.136
When I'm 16...

946
00:54:25.775 --> 00:54:27.744
There you are sweetheart.

947
00:54:27.775 --> 00:54:29.344
Mom don't you ever knock?

948
00:54:29.374 --> 00:54:30.544
I need privacy.

949
00:54:30.574 --> 00:54:31.573
What?

950
00:54:31.613 --> 00:54:33.971
I need privacy.

951
00:54:34.011 --> 00:54:35.112
Hold on a minute.

952
00:54:35.142 --> 00:54:37.041
Bob come here a minute.

953
00:54:37.071 --> 00:54:38.541
Tell your dad.

954
00:54:38.581 --> 00:54:40.380
I need privacy.

955
00:54:40.410 --> 00:54:41.510
One more time.

956
00:54:41.550 --> 00:54:43.009
I need privacy.
I need privacy.

957
00:54:43.049 --> 00:54:44.849
I don't understand a word
she's saying. Do you?

958
00:54:44.879 --> 00:54:46.948
No. Then again I never do.

959
00:54:54.316 --> 00:54:56.015
This has to work.

960
00:55:11.390 --> 00:55:13.190
Please understand.

961
00:55:25.196 --> 00:55:26.905
Abby!
Hi Daddy.

962
00:55:26.935 --> 00:55:29.104
Honey look who it is.

963
00:55:29.134 --> 00:55:31.204
Hello sweetheart.
Hi Mom.

964
00:55:31.234 --> 00:55:34.073
Shouldn't you be at your own
place unpacking those boxes?

965
00:55:34.103 --> 00:55:36.743
Yeah but I missed you guys.

966
00:55:36.773 --> 00:55:38.341
Aw that's sweet.

967
00:55:38.371 --> 00:55:40.071
But we're kind
of busy right now.

968
00:55:40.111 --> 00:55:41.480
Your turn dear.

969
00:55:41.510 --> 00:55:42.780
What's the use?

970
00:55:42.810 --> 00:55:45.610
22 cards in my hand
and I still can't play!

971
00:55:48.978 --> 00:55:49.848
Can't this wait?

972
00:55:49.878 --> 00:55:52.118
Of course it can.

973
00:55:52.148 --> 00:55:53.816
What's up?

974
00:55:56.585 --> 00:55:58.885
Well um...

975
00:56:00.155 --> 00:56:03.194
I have something
important to discuss with you

976
00:56:03.224 --> 00:56:10.861
and I thought if you really listen
to me you might understand.

977
00:56:13.700 --> 00:56:14.660
Bob.

978
00:56:14.700 --> 00:56:16.969
What? I'm listening.

979
00:56:16.999 --> 00:56:19.068
We're listening.

980
00:56:19.098 --> 00:56:20.398
Even if it sounds crazy?

981
00:56:20.438 --> 00:56:22.667
I listen to your father
all the time.

982
00:56:22.707 --> 00:56:23.667
What's that supposed to mean?

983
00:56:23.707 --> 00:56:25.236
Go on sweetheart.

984
00:56:29.275 --> 00:56:33.244
When I woke up this morning
I was 16 years old.

985
00:56:36.782 --> 00:56:39.742
I thought this was going to be
the best day of my life.

986
00:56:39.782 --> 00:56:45.680
Then this Birthday Fairy
appeared and gave me these.

987
00:56:48.549 --> 00:56:52.788
Would you look at this hon.

988
00:56:52.828 --> 00:56:55.487
Well that brings back
memories doesn't it?

989
00:56:55.527 --> 00:56:57.596
What?
What memories?

990
00:56:57.626 --> 00:57:00.295
Your father took me to the
Lucky Duck Chinese Restaurant

991
00:57:00.325 --> 00:57:02.264
on the night you were born.

992
00:57:02.294 --> 00:57:04.094
I had the orange chicken.

993
00:57:04.134 --> 00:57:05.094
We thought it was an omen.

994
00:57:05.134 --> 00:57:07.134
We always felt so lucky

995
00:57:07.164 --> 00:57:10.302
to have a daughter as
wonderful as you are.

996
00:57:10.332 --> 00:57:11.431
Really?

997
00:57:11.471 --> 00:57:13.232
Really.

998
00:57:15.841 --> 00:57:20.308
Then you'll understand when
I say I need to come back

999
00:57:20.338 --> 00:57:22.509
and live with you
and go back to school..

1000
00:57:22.539 --> 00:57:25.847
I'm not ready to have my own
apartment and my own job.

1001
00:57:25.877 --> 00:57:27.846
Please tell me you understand.

1002
00:57:27.876 --> 00:57:33.385
Abby look behind you.

1003
00:57:33.415 --> 00:57:34.784
Ever since you were
a little girl

1004
00:57:34.814 --> 00:57:38.953
all you wanted was to be
exactly what you are now.

1005
00:57:38.983 --> 00:57:43.691
Beautiful and independent.

1006
00:57:43.721 --> 00:57:45.990
I remember the day
this photo was taken.

1007
00:57:46.030 --> 00:57:48.829
You wanted a grown-up
birthday party.

1008
00:57:48.859 --> 00:57:53.068
All dressed up in my
high heels and pearls.

1009
00:57:53.098 --> 00:57:54.599
You were never happier.

1010
00:57:54.629 --> 00:57:59.436
But being grown up is different
than dreaming about it isn't it?

1011
00:57:59.466 --> 00:58:02.136
Yes.

1012
00:58:02.176 --> 00:58:04.034
We understand you.

1013
00:58:04.074 --> 00:58:05.704
You do?

1014
00:58:05.744 --> 00:58:07.144
Of course.

1015
00:58:07.174 --> 00:58:08.744
You're scared your childhood
is over and with it

1016
00:58:08.774 --> 00:58:11.972
all the best times of your life.
Yes!

1017
00:58:12.012 --> 00:58:13.782
You probably want to just turn
back the clock and start over.

1018
00:58:13.812 --> 00:58:14.842
Yes! Yes!

1019
00:58:14.882 --> 00:58:16.281
That's exactly
what I want to do!

1020
00:58:16.311 --> 00:58:19.579
We know how that feels.

1021
00:58:19.619 --> 00:58:22.749
Then I'm still your
little girl?

1022
00:58:22.779 --> 00:58:25.388
You'll always be our
little girl Pumpkin...

1023
00:58:35.764 --> 00:58:37.424
Look! Wasps!

1024
00:58:37.464 --> 00:58:38.363
Time to go Pumpkin.

1025
00:58:38.393 --> 00:58:40.193
Drive safe.

1026
00:58:40.233 --> 00:58:41.862
And don't forget these.

1027
00:58:41.902 --> 00:58:44.331
But I thought you
guys understood.

1028
00:58:44.361 --> 00:58:46.571
We do understand Adulthood
could be tough.

1029
00:58:46.601 --> 00:58:48.430
Sometimes it gets
a little buggy.

1030
00:58:48.470 --> 00:58:50.469
Bye now sweetheart!

1031
00:58:52.670 --> 00:58:54.109
Love you!

1032
00:58:59.346 --> 00:59:01.646
So that's what that feels like.

1033
00:59:30.128 --> 00:59:31.227
Hi Logan.

1034
00:59:31.267 --> 00:59:32.367
Hey.

1035
00:59:32.397 --> 00:59:33.636
Cool ride.

1036
00:59:33.666 --> 00:59:36.336
Yeah you said that
this morning.

1037
00:59:36.366 --> 00:59:37.964
Huh?

1038
00:59:38.004 --> 00:59:42.173
So...what are you
doing here?

1039
00:59:42.203 --> 00:59:43.903
Party.

1040
00:59:43.943 --> 00:59:45.741
Right.

1041
00:59:47.712 --> 00:59:50.511
I wasn't invited.

1042
00:59:50.541 --> 00:59:51.710
Huh.

1043
00:59:57.178 --> 00:59:58.978
Hey!
Yeah?

1044
00:59:59.018 --> 01:00:01.047
Will you do something for me?
Sure.

1045
01:00:01.087 --> 01:00:03.886
Take a picture of me
with your car.

1046
01:00:03.916 --> 01:00:06.325
Okay.

1047
01:00:06.355 --> 01:00:07.625
Thanks.

1048
01:00:07.655 --> 01:00:09.424
It's what I want
when I'm your age.

1049
01:00:13.363 --> 01:00:14.822
There ya go.

1050
01:00:14.862 --> 01:00:16.263
Cool.

1051
01:00:18.031 --> 01:00:20.700
Oh man that's hot.

1052
01:00:20.730 --> 01:00:22.531
I can't wait to show Krista!

1053
01:00:39.115 --> 01:00:40.515
Joey Lockhart!

1054
01:00:43.354 --> 01:00:45.413
Get off of me!

1055
01:00:45.453 --> 01:00:46.882
Get off!

1056
01:00:46.922 --> 01:00:48.352
You have to believe me Jay.

1057
01:00:48.382 --> 01:00:49.721
You're my best friend and
it's my 16th birthday

1058
01:00:49.751 --> 01:00:51.821
and I got these magic
candles at the bus stop

1059
01:00:51.851 --> 01:00:54.250
and this big car pulled up
and Joey Lockhart got out

1060
01:00:54.290 --> 01:00:59.258
and kissed me... I don't know her.

1061
01:00:59.288 --> 01:01:01.157
You were there!
You saw him!

1062
01:01:01.187 --> 01:01:02.728
Let go.

1063
01:01:02.758 --> 01:01:06.056
Not until you listen to me.
Give me five minutes.

1064
01:01:10.064 --> 01:01:11.565
Four.

1065
01:01:15.703 --> 01:01:17.733
Okay.

1066
01:01:17.773 --> 01:01:20.071
I know this is hard to believe

1067
01:01:20.101 --> 01:01:24.041
but we're best friends
and I can prove it.

1068
01:01:26.680 --> 01:01:28.009
So?

1069
01:01:28.039 --> 01:01:30.238
Look at your key ring.

1070
01:01:50.961 --> 01:01:54.091
"Happy Sweet 16. Love Jay."

1071
01:01:56.160 --> 01:01:58.000
You gave this to
me this morning.

1072
01:01:58.030 --> 01:02:00.228
For my 16th birthday.

1073
01:02:13.205 --> 01:02:14.064
Abby.

1074
01:02:14.104 --> 01:02:16.074
You remember?

1075
01:02:16.104 --> 01:02:18.003
I think so.

1076
01:02:18.043 --> 01:02:20.972
So you believe me?

1077
01:02:21.002 --> 01:02:23.141
Yeah.

1078
01:02:23.171 --> 01:02:24.541
I do.

1079
01:02:35.177 --> 01:02:36.547
He believes me!

1080
01:02:36.577 --> 01:02:37.776
Whoa.

1081
01:02:37.816 --> 01:02:39.187
Volume.

1082
01:02:43.614 --> 01:02:46.483
This doesn't change anything.

1083
01:02:46.523 --> 01:02:51.392
And when midnight comes
I'm stuck like this forever.

1084
01:02:58.660 --> 01:03:00.989
Here lemme see the list.

1085
01:03:01.029 --> 01:03:03.888
Here ya go.

1086
01:03:03.928 --> 01:03:13.265
Okay you've used 1 2
7 8 9... Skip ahead.

1087
01:03:13.305 --> 01:03:15.204
I can't believe
you wasted a wish on sushi.

1088
01:03:15.234 --> 01:03:16.835
I was 8.

1089
01:03:16.875 --> 01:03:19.304
I had a very
unsophisticated palate.

1090
01:03:19.334 --> 01:03:20.902
Had?

1091
01:03:27.111 --> 01:03:30.109
You're a great best friend Jay.

1092
01:03:30.139 --> 01:03:33.609
I know.

1093
01:03:33.649 --> 01:03:34.849
C'mon.

1094
01:03:34.879 --> 01:03:38.048
Most of these are
kind of useless

1095
01:03:38.078 --> 01:03:40.747
since you're already an adult.

1096
01:03:40.787 --> 01:03:48.184
That leaves 15 and Logan
Buchanan... Yeah about that...

1097
01:03:48.224 --> 01:03:51.153
15 was always my favorite.

1098
01:03:51.193 --> 01:03:55.791
"When I'm 16 I'll have
the best party ever."

1099
01:04:00.130 --> 01:04:03.799
But you're not 16 anymore.

1100
01:04:15.906 --> 01:04:17.634
Hey.

1101
01:04:17.674 --> 01:04:21.373
I kinda have to make an
appearance at Krista's party.

1102
01:04:21.403 --> 01:04:24.942
Do you maybe want to come
with me?

1103
01:04:27.612 --> 01:04:28.981
Not as my date or anything.

1104
01:04:29.011 --> 01:04:30.351
No.

1105
01:04:30.380 --> 01:04:33.149
Of course not.

1106
01:04:33.189 --> 01:04:34.789
Well?

1107
01:04:39.258 --> 01:04:41.157
I'd love to go with you Jay.

1108
01:04:43.326 --> 01:04:45.126
Okay.

1109
01:04:55.793 --> 01:04:58.061
Sync by Hana.Bean
www.Addic7ed.Com

1110
01:05:02.031 --> 01:05:03.530
Great party.

1111
01:05:03.560 --> 01:05:05.598
Ladies first.

1112
01:05:17.166 --> 01:05:19.605
Mike?

1113
01:05:19.635 --> 01:05:21.704
Give a shout-out to my
big sis Abby everybody.

1114
01:05:25.633 --> 01:05:27.902
You're super old Abs
but you're still cool!

1115
01:05:27.942 --> 01:05:29.841
So Mike can really play?

1116
01:05:29.871 --> 01:05:31.041
Yeah.

1117
01:05:31.071 --> 01:05:32.700
Something just clicked
with him this year.

1118
01:05:32.740 --> 01:05:34.641
He got serious about
playing guitar.

1119
01:05:34.670 --> 01:05:36.839
He's getting paid really
well for this gig.

1120
01:05:42.478 --> 01:05:43.407
Wait.

1121
01:05:43.437 --> 01:05:44.606
Did I miss something?

1122
01:05:44.636 --> 01:05:46.805
I mean besides senior year?

1123
01:05:46.835 --> 01:05:49.404
Jay you're here!

1124
01:05:49.444 --> 01:05:52.044
Hi! I'm so glad
you could make it!

1125
01:05:52.074 --> 01:05:53.604
Yeah.

1126
01:05:53.644 --> 01:05:56.543
I'm...Abby Jensen.

1127
01:05:56.583 --> 01:05:57.843
I know silly.

1128
01:05:57.883 --> 01:05:59.842
We're neighbors?

1129
01:05:59.882 --> 01:06:02.751
Yes.
Neighbors.

1130
01:06:02.781 --> 01:06:04.280
Your party looks awesome.

1131
01:06:04.310 --> 01:06:06.280
Thanks to your parents.

1132
01:06:06.320 --> 01:06:08.378
They found all these amazing
decorations in their garage

1133
01:06:08.418 --> 01:06:10.548
after their house
was infested by wasps.

1134
01:06:10.588 --> 01:06:13.617
I guess they were left over
from your Sweet 16 Party

1135
01:06:13.657 --> 01:06:15.586
but never got used
for some reason.

1136
01:06:15.626 --> 01:06:17.696
So they just gave them to me!

1137
01:06:17.726 --> 01:06:18.795
Lucky you.

1138
01:06:18.825 --> 01:06:20.895
I know right?

1139
01:06:20.925 --> 01:06:24.193
And you're just in time
for the big celebration.

1140
01:06:26.763 --> 01:06:27.902
Thanks for coming everybody!

1141
01:06:32.572 --> 01:06:34.510
Man this is a dream
come true for me.

1142
01:06:36.080 --> 01:06:37.340
What's happening?

1143
01:06:37.380 --> 01:06:38.479
Jay Kepler
ladies and gentlemen.

1144
01:06:38.509 --> 01:06:40.708
Our new Student Body President!

1145
01:06:46.117 --> 01:06:47.646
Thank you.

1146
01:06:47.686 --> 01:06:50.046
I want to recognize my campaign
manager Krista Cook.

1147
01:06:53.914 --> 01:06:55.684
What all of you don't know is
that I really wanted this

1148
01:06:55.724 --> 01:06:58.353
but I was too afraid to try.

1149
01:06:58.393 --> 01:06:59.892
I couldn't have done it
without your help Krista.

1150
01:07:01.722 --> 01:07:04.621
Thank you so much!

1151
01:07:04.661 --> 01:07:08.529
1 2 3 4...
Have fun okay? Mm-hmm.

1152
01:07:14.767 --> 01:07:17.366
So you're Student Body
President?

1153
01:07:17.396 --> 01:07:18.697
Yep.

1154
01:07:18.737 --> 01:07:21.606
I was Student Body President.

1155
01:07:21.636 --> 01:07:22.965
Oh yeah.

1156
01:07:23.005 --> 01:07:24.304
Weird.

1157
01:07:24.334 --> 01:07:27.003
I thought with me out of the
way Krista would win for sure.

1158
01:07:27.043 --> 01:07:28.602
Krista?

1159
01:07:28.642 --> 01:07:31.002
She's hates competition.

1160
01:07:31.042 --> 01:07:32.101
Krista?

1161
01:07:32.141 --> 01:07:33.341
Our Krista.

1162
01:07:33.371 --> 01:07:34.441
Yeah.

1163
01:07:34.471 --> 01:07:36.211
I think without you in her life

1164
01:07:36.241 --> 01:07:39.310
she just didn't have a reason
to compete for anything.

1165
01:07:39.340 --> 01:07:43.438
She's kind super helpful a good
listener and a great friend.

1166
01:07:43.478 --> 01:07:45.648
You guys would like each other.

1167
01:07:45.678 --> 01:07:48.517
If y'know you were
the same age right?

1168
01:08:09.829 --> 01:08:12.799
♪ Look around it's dead of night ♪

1169
01:08:12.829 --> 01:08:16.067
♪ You've been losing every fight ♪

1170
01:08:16.097 --> 01:08:20.936
♪ Your hope is feeling broken ♪

1171
01:08:20.976 --> 01:08:22.475
♪ Your feet are rough ♪

1172
01:08:22.505 --> 01:08:24.445
♪ They're scraped and bruised ♪

1173
01:08:24.475 --> 01:08:28.474
♪ But still have strength
to take you through ♪

1174
01:08:28.514 --> 01:08:33.282
♪ Into the dawn ♪

1175
01:08:33.312 --> 01:08:35.551
♪ Just close your eyes ♪

1176
01:08:35.581 --> 01:08:36.951
This was supposed
to be my party.

1177
01:08:36.981 --> 01:08:38.620
♪ ...and push right through ♪

1178
01:08:38.650 --> 01:08:41.490
♪ I know it's tough right now ♪

1179
01:08:41.520 --> 01:08:44.818
♪ This was meant for you ♪

1180
01:08:44.858 --> 01:08:47.557
♪ When the clouds are gone ♪

1181
01:08:47.597 --> 01:08:50.726
♪ Not a shadow in sight ♪

1182
01:08:50.766 --> 01:08:56.735
♪ You'll be drenched in the sun
with open eyes ♪

1183
01:08:56.775 --> 01:08:59.204
♪ Oh oh oh... ♪

1184
01:09:02.672 --> 01:09:05.482
♪ Oh oh oh... ♪

1185
01:09:08.581 --> 01:09:10.880
♪ Now at the beach the waves still crash ♪

1186
01:09:10.910 --> 01:09:14.549
♪ The tide can grab and pull you back ♪

1187
01:09:14.579 --> 01:09:19.617
♪ And the sun may be covered in gray ♪

1188
01:09:19.657 --> 01:09:22.486
♪ The sand will itch the salt can burn ♪

1189
01:09:22.516 --> 01:09:26.825
♪ The hurricane will take its turn ♪

1190
01:09:26.855 --> 01:09:31.423
♪ Until the dawn ♪

1191
01:09:31.463 --> 01:09:36.932
♪ Just close your eyes and push
right through ♪

1192
01:09:36.972 --> 01:09:40.100
♪ I know it's tough right now ♪

1193
01:09:40.140 --> 01:09:43.110
♪ This was meant for you ♪

1194
01:09:43.140 --> 01:09:46.038
♪ When the clouds are gone ♪

1195
01:09:46.078 --> 01:09:49.178
♪ Not a storm in sight ♪

1196
01:09:49.218 --> 01:09:52.077
♪ You'll be drenched in the sun ♪

1197
01:09:52.117 --> 01:09:55.315
♪ With open eyes ♪

1198
01:10:18.668 --> 01:10:21.267
♪ So close your eyes shut them tight ♪

1199
01:10:21.297 --> 01:10:26.605
♪ Let it be and it will fade away ♪

1200
01:10:26.635 --> 01:10:28.774
♪ Fade away ♪

1201
01:10:30.445 --> 01:10:33.144
♪ Push on through there's strength in you ♪

1202
01:10:33.174 --> 01:10:37.771
♪ Let it be and wish it all away ♪

1203
01:10:37.811 --> 01:10:40.181
♪ All away ♪

1204
01:10:42.011 --> 01:10:45.050
♪ So close your eyes shut them tight ♪

1205
01:10:45.080 --> 01:10:48.989
♪ Let it be and it will fade away ♪

1206
01:10:53.227 --> 01:10:56.886
♪ Push on through there's strength in you ♪

1207
01:10:56.926 --> 01:11:00.295
♪ Let it be and wish it all away ♪

1208
01:11:05.534 --> 01:11:09.162
♪ With open eyes opened wide it's all good ♪

1209
01:11:09.202 --> 01:11:13.531
♪ Now watch it fade away ♪

1210
01:11:13.571 --> 01:11:16.769
♪ Day by day ♪

1211
01:11:16.799 --> 01:11:22.208
♪ Just close your eyes and push
right through ♪

1212
01:11:22.238 --> 01:11:25.637
♪ I know it's tough right now ♪

1213
01:11:25.677 --> 01:11:28.576
♪ But this was meant for you ♪

1214
01:11:28.606 --> 01:11:34.343
♪ When the clouds are gone
not a storm in sight ♪

1215
01:11:34.384 --> 01:11:40.282
♪ You'll be drenched in the sun
with open eyes ♪

1216
01:11:49.530 --> 01:11:52.189
Large pepperoni pineapple
for Jensen.

1217
01:12:00.125 --> 01:12:01.795
I didn't order a pizza.

1218
01:12:01.825 --> 01:12:03.094
I know.

1219
01:12:03.124 --> 01:12:05.864
I just thought
you could use a friend.

1220
01:12:08.993 --> 01:12:10.332
Oh sweetie.

1221
01:12:13.631 --> 01:12:15.331
Dry those tears.

1222
01:12:17.030 --> 01:12:18.430
I'm starving.

1223
01:12:18.470 --> 01:12:19.869
You are?

1224
01:12:19.899 --> 01:12:23.338
Sure us magical beings
have to eat too.

1225
01:12:24.738 --> 01:12:26.637
This day didn't go
like I thought it would.

1226
01:12:26.667 --> 01:12:28.337
I can't believe I wasted
my wishes on things

1227
01:12:28.366 --> 01:12:29.706
like beating Krista Cook.

1228
01:12:29.736 --> 01:12:31.235
Yeah.

1229
01:12:31.275 --> 01:12:34.504
She's pretty nice now that she
is not out to destroy you.

1230
01:12:34.545 --> 01:12:35.744
Don't rub it in.

1231
01:12:35.774 --> 01:12:37.873
She's a really good friend
to Jay.

1232
01:12:37.913 --> 01:12:39.544
Better than I was.

1233
01:12:39.574 --> 01:12:42.143
I didn't even know he wanted
to be Student Body President.

1234
01:12:42.183 --> 01:12:44.481
How could I have been
so thoughtless?

1235
01:12:46.111 --> 01:12:47.381
All I could think about

1236
01:12:47.411 --> 01:12:52.219
was having parties and
clothes and popularity.

1237
01:12:52.249 --> 01:12:55.477
I can't believe those things
were so important to me.

1238
01:12:55.517 --> 01:12:57.148
You were 16.

1239
01:12:57.188 --> 01:12:59.087
But I didn't appreciate it.

1240
01:12:59.117 --> 01:13:01.786
Ever since I was little
I wanted to grow up.

1241
01:13:01.816 --> 01:13:06.254
I thought it was the only way
to get what I wanted.

1242
01:13:06.294 --> 01:13:09.653
I guess I didn't realize
what I already had.

1243
01:13:21.599 --> 01:13:24.098
You still have
this little number.

1244
01:13:29.837 --> 01:13:31.876
Wish 16.

1245
01:13:31.906 --> 01:13:35.175
All those years I saved it
for something really special.

1246
01:13:38.303 --> 01:13:40.144
Of all the wishes on this list

1247
01:13:40.174 --> 01:13:43.543
this is the one
I wish I could change.

1248
01:13:57.088 --> 01:13:59.087
Wow that gum is still
really fresh.

1249
01:14:13.923 --> 01:14:13.963
Maybe the rules
don't know about gum.

1250
01:14:15.891 --> 01:14:18.331
There's only one way
to find out.

1251
01:14:44.683 --> 01:14:49.081
I wish I could start
this whole day over again.

1252
01:14:54.349 --> 01:14:55.519
Surprise!

1253
01:14:59.857 --> 01:15:01.628
Happy Birthday Abby.

1254
01:15:01.657 --> 01:15:02.687
Look.

1255
01:15:02.727 --> 01:15:04.726
Your first 16th
birthday picture.

1256
01:15:09.265 --> 01:15:11.834
This is a great picture!

1257
01:15:11.864 --> 01:15:14.562
This is the best picture I've
ever seen in my entire life!

1258
01:15:14.602 --> 01:15:16.263
Thank you thank you thank you!

1259
01:15:16.303 --> 01:15:18.172
You're welcome Pumpkin.

1260
01:15:19.701 --> 01:15:21.871
Make a wish sweetheart?

1261
01:15:21.901 --> 01:15:25.040
I wish for exactly this.

1262
01:15:25.070 --> 01:15:27.969
Everything is perfect.

1263
01:15:32.277 --> 01:15:33.707
Wasps!

1264
01:15:34.776 --> 01:15:35.776
Yeah.

1265
01:15:38.175 --> 01:15:40.076
I saw one crawl up the AC vent.

1266
01:15:40.116 --> 01:15:41.485
No not one. Thousands!

1267
01:15:41.515 --> 01:15:44.144
Nesting up there for 16 years!

1268
01:15:44.183 --> 01:15:45.983
Sweetheart we know.

1269
01:15:46.013 --> 01:15:47.683
No you don't know.
You can't possibly know

1270
01:15:47.713 --> 01:15:49.282
that the house is going
to be totally infested

1271
01:15:49.321 --> 01:15:50.851
and the wasps will
take over the cars

1272
01:15:50.881 --> 01:15:53.021
and you and Dad'll have
to live in the driveway

1273
01:15:53.051 --> 01:15:54.889
but then Joey Lockhart
will come and kiss me

1274
01:15:54.919 --> 01:15:56.319
and I will get candles
and wishes

1275
01:15:56.360 --> 01:15:58.289
and some really
gorgeous clothes

1276
01:15:58.329 --> 01:16:01.027
and everything will look
like it will be okay.

1277
01:16:01.067 --> 01:16:02.397
But then I will make
a really stupid wish

1278
01:16:02.427 --> 01:16:03.867
that I didn't mean to make

1279
01:16:03.907 --> 01:16:06.206
and I will have to grow up and
live alone and miss my party

1280
01:16:06.236 --> 01:16:07.766
and this will turn into
the worst 16th birthday

1281
01:16:07.806 --> 01:16:09.405
in the history of
16th birthdays!

1282
01:16:09.435 --> 01:16:12.145
You have to call
the exterminator now!

1283
01:16:15.673 --> 01:16:17.113
Okey dokey.

1284
01:16:17.143 --> 01:16:18.482
All done.

1285
01:16:18.512 --> 01:16:21.412
Whoo that was some wasps' nest.

1286
01:16:21.452 --> 01:16:22.551
Celeste?

1287
01:16:22.581 --> 01:16:23.611
Hi Abby.

1288
01:16:23.651 --> 01:16:24.880
You know her.

1289
01:16:24.920 --> 01:16:27.720
Yeah we just met this morning.

1290
01:16:27.750 --> 01:16:31.358
When Abby called me.
You're very lucky I showed up when I did.

1291
01:16:31.388 --> 01:16:34.487
So the wasps are all gone.

1292
01:16:34.527 --> 01:16:37.326
Like they never happened.

1293
01:16:37.356 --> 01:16:39.556
Everything is going to be okay?

1294
01:16:39.595 --> 01:16:41.925
Better than okay.

1295
01:16:41.965 --> 01:16:43.964
Wait.
What do I owe ya?

1296
01:16:43.995 --> 01:16:46.163
Consider it a Sweet 16 gift.

1297
01:16:46.203 --> 01:16:48.433
Happy Birthday Abby.

1298
01:16:48.463 --> 01:16:49.703
Thank you.

1299
01:16:49.733 --> 01:16:52.232
For everything.

1300
01:16:57.410 --> 01:17:00.439
Go on down and start making that
special birthday breakfast

1301
01:17:00.479 --> 01:17:01.609
you have planned for me Mom.

1302
01:17:01.639 --> 01:17:03.038
I'll be right there.

1303
01:17:28.559 --> 01:17:32.299
♪ Da na na da na na now! ♪

1304
01:17:34.328 --> 01:17:37.566
♪ Da na na da na na now! ♪

1305
01:17:37.596 --> 01:17:38.697
Hey!

1306
01:17:38.737 --> 01:17:39.836
This is for you.

1307
01:17:39.866 --> 01:17:41.736
I was saving it
for my Sweet 16 party

1308
01:17:41.766 --> 01:17:45.105
but I think you need it more.

1309
01:17:45.135 --> 01:17:46.034
Whoa!

1310
01:17:46.074 --> 01:17:48.344
For what?

1311
01:17:48.373 --> 01:17:49.773
A real guitar.

1312
01:17:49.813 --> 01:17:52.442
I think you're really talented.

1313
01:17:56.812 --> 01:17:58.280
Thank you Abs.

1314
01:17:59.650 --> 01:18:00.979
I love you Mike.

1315
01:18:04.188 --> 01:18:06.587
Thanks for the yummy
breakfast Mom and Dad.

1316
01:18:06.617 --> 01:18:08.916
Love you!

1317
01:18:11.626 --> 01:18:13.925
Love you too.

1318
01:18:13.955 --> 01:18:16.524
Krista! Krista! Wait!

1319
01:18:16.564 --> 01:18:17.465
Get back.

1320
01:18:17.493 --> 01:18:18.923
We need to talk.

1321
01:18:18.963 --> 01:18:21.632
I have nothing to say to you.

1322
01:18:21.662 --> 01:18:23.862
I have one quick question.

1323
01:18:23.902 --> 01:18:26.271
No you cannot have a ride.

1324
01:18:26.301 --> 01:18:28.171
I don't want a ride.

1325
01:18:28.201 --> 01:18:30.940
I want to understand.

1326
01:18:30.970 --> 01:18:32.938
What did I ever do to you?

1327
01:18:32.968 --> 01:18:34.709
Go away.

1328
01:18:34.739 --> 01:18:36.008
No.

1329
01:18:36.038 --> 01:18:38.977
Not until you answer me.

1330
01:18:39.007 --> 01:18:40.648
Why don't you like me?

1331
01:18:43.546 --> 01:18:45.646
You really don't know do you?

1332
01:18:45.676 --> 01:18:48.644
Not a clue.

1333
01:18:55.282 --> 01:18:57.751
It was in third grade.

1334
01:18:57.791 --> 01:19:00.490
Jay and I were best friends.

1335
01:19:00.520 --> 01:19:04.058
Then you moved to town.

1336
01:19:04.088 --> 01:19:06.988
It was my birthday.

1337
01:19:07.028 --> 01:19:09.798
Jay and I made a pact...

1338
01:19:13.095 --> 01:19:15.965
Cheese!

1339
01:19:15.995 --> 01:19:17.195
Best friends forever!

1340
01:19:17.235 --> 01:19:19.064
Yeah!

1341
01:19:28.941 --> 01:19:30.101
I stole your best friend.

1342
01:19:30.141 --> 01:19:33.110
On my birthday.

1343
01:19:33.140 --> 01:19:36.508
After that Jay and I
did everything together.

1344
01:19:36.548 --> 01:19:38.379
Without me.

1345
01:19:38.409 --> 01:19:40.808
That must have been
so horrible for you.

1346
01:19:40.848 --> 01:19:42.876
It was.

1347
01:19:42.916 --> 01:19:45.145
I can't imagine how you felt.

1348
01:19:45.185 --> 01:19:47.316
